[en.C01_DESC]
After the Ultimate Battle, Cozy Glow, one of the “Big Three” has taken over Equestria according to the Canterlot Pact, crowning herself as the “Empress of Friendship”, establishing the Equestria Empire.
However, the young Cozy Glow is unable to control the entire Equestria Empire. In such embarrassing situation, war and revolutions are everywhere, Cozy Glow is forced to implement the feudal system in the Equestria Empire. The Duchy of Ponyville, the Duchy of Cloudsdale, the Dominion of Appaloosa and other territories are separated from the Empire and handed over to local forces for autonomy. The Starlight Liberation Front, the Discord Legion and the Free Equestria, who refuse to recognize the new Empire, are all marching towards Canterlot. Although the Crystal Empire is currently controlled by the Unity Commission appointed by the Equestria Empire, the Changeling Empire is constantly trying to exert political influence and change the status quo of the Crystal Empire. Las Pegasus, Equestria Education Association and Sire’s Hollow all have their own plans.
How will Empress Cozy Glow maintain this so-called “Empire” that is shattered into pieces?

[en.PIHC_WS_C01_desc]
At the end of year 999, Cozy Glow, Queen Chrysalis, and Lord Tirek, known as the “Big Three”, defeated M6 in the Ultimate Battle, and then they went on to defeat the resistance forces all over Equestria. After more than a year of war, the “Big Three” returned to Canterlot and signed the Canterlot Pact, which established the new order after the war. The Pact explicitly divided the jurisdiction of the “Big Three”: Cozy Glow would establish the Equestria Empire and become the Empress; Queen Chrysalis would revert the changelings back to its original un-hatched state, restore the rule and expand the territory of the Changeling Empire; and Lord Tirek would lead the centaurs to take over the Griffonica continent.
However, according to informed sources, the negotiation process of the Canterlot Pact was not easy. The “Big Three” argued incessantly during the week-long meeting, and even almost came to blows. Nevertheless, the three eventually reached a consensus and presented a united front to the outside world, declaring the arrival of a new era in the world of Equestria.
Cozy Glow, as the weakest of the “Big Three” in terms of magic, did not gain any advantage in the negotiation process, instead had to make concessions again and again. Cozy Glow who was good at politics, was well aware that her power was not enough to manage the entire Equestria, and she had to rely on the help and support of the other two. However, help and support would never come without a price. Rumor has it that the public Canterlot Pact is just a superficially bright and beautiful declaration, a hypocritical agreement. The real agreement reached by the “Big Three” contains a large number of clauses that violate the will of the ponies, such as handing the Crystal Empire over to the changelings. Cozy Glow was quite unhappy about this after returning to the palace from the Canterlot Pact talks, and ordered the suppression of all reports that did not conform to the content of the Canterlot Pact.

In the summer of 1002, after careful and long preparation, the formal coronation ceremony of Empress Cozy Glow finally arrived.
The scene of the coronation ceremony was magnificent and luxurious:
The empress’s robe and crown were even heavier than herself, so she could only sit on the throne carried by more than twenty flying horses to complete her Canterlot parade.
The parade route was crowded with welcoming little ponies and a few other species living in Canterlot. The little ponies danced with flowers and fireworks in their hands, shouting loudly welcoming words such as “Long live Empress Cozy Glow!” “Long live the Empress!” “The Empress rules for a thousand years!” “The gospel of Eqeustria has come!” “Great Empress!” and “Is it over? Where can I reimburse the fireworks?” “Is the degree of this smile qualified? Will it be unnatural?”, etc.
“Empress Cozy Glow was so welcomed that there were enthusiastic little ponies waving their hooves to hug the Empress all the way.” - The Equestria Empire Daily reported, for which the organizers of the coronation ceremony had to use the entire security force of Canterlot to maintain order on the scene; after the coronation ceremony, tens of thousands of ponies listened to the speech of Empress Cozy Glow, and then performed programs for Empress Cozy Glow in an organized manner.
It is said that during the carnival after the coronation ceremony, the entire Canterlot was repainted into a shiny gold, covering a large number of obscene graffiti on the streets by a few unfriendly residents.
After the coronation ceremony, even the street lights were all replaced with ancient artifacts full of magic (unfortunately, after the end of the coronation ceremony, more than a dozen “street lights” were stolen and their whereabouts are still unknown).
Queen Chrysalis and Lord Tirek were also invited to attend the coronation ceremony of Empress Cozy Glow and delivered speeches on the spot: “The coronation of Empress Cozy Glow, who is respected and loved, symbolizes the eternal friendship of the changelings, ponies, and centaurs!” - Lord Tirek said so, and Queen Chrysalis also agreed. The day after the coronation ceremony, Queen Chrysalis and Lord Tirek, who stayed in Canterlot, met with the newly enthroned Empress Cozy Glow again and discussed the implementation of the Canterlot Pact over the past year, resolving some misunderstandings and disputes. Queen Chrysalis said that as a gesture of today’s tri-racial friendship, it is necessary to redefine some of the terms of the pact. The revised agreement of the Canterlot Pact after the meeting was not made public, but Empress Cozy Glow went to bed early that night, did not talk to other ponies, and even did not had her dinner, presumably because of exhaustion from busy political affairs.

After the coronation ceremony, the newly established Equestria Empire also returned to its former calm. In order to prepare for this coronation ceremony, and to govern Equestria, which was in a state of disrepair due to the previous war, Empress Cozy Glow had been busy for months, sometimes working so hard that she stayed up all night. The government affairs of the Empire have increased rather than decreased, so some new government members suggested that the empress should delegate the affairs to government members and localities, but the empress was unable to trust this temporary government and loose local governments, insisting on handling all affairs personally to prevent the conspiracy of others. According to an unnamed servant pony around the empress, since the coronation ceremony, the empress has been somewhat silent, for reasons unknown. It may be that the heavy work and the fear of rebellion are gradually devouring her soul, but there are also claims that she is just missing her mother.

In the new world after the Canterlot Pact came into effect, apart from occasional meetings, the “Big Three” ruled their respective territories independently. Empress Cozy Glow, who lost the support of the other two giants, was unable to eliminate all the resistance forces with her own power and the new imperial government. After negotiations with representatives of influential and willing to cooperate with the imperial government in various regions, Empress Cozy Glow had to accept the proposal to implement the feudal system in the Equestria Empire. Therefore, various regions have a great deal of autonomy in the form of fiefdoms, autonomous territories, and independent organizations.

From Cloudsdale in the north to the Rock Farm in the south, from Manehattan in the east to Sire’s Hollow in the west, it seems that there is no land that is completely loyal to the Empire. How will Empress Cozy Glow maintain this so-called “Empire” that is shattered into pieces?

